      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Headquarters Trap: IRDAI is headquartered in Hyderabad, whereas RBI and SEBI are based in Mumbai.",
        "Statutory vs Non-Statutory: SEBI was non-statutory when formed in 1988 and gained statutory status in 1992.",
        "Apex Functions: RBI acts as the lender of last resort, SEBI regulates stock exchanges, and IRDAI mandates solvency margins for insurers."
      ],
      "id": "udf2ojq"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "RBI regulates the banking sector, monetary policy, and foreign exchange reserves under the RBI Act, 1934.",
        "SEBI oversees the capital and securities markets to protect investor interests under the SEBI Act, 1992.",
        "IRDAI regulates and promotes the insurance and reinsurance industry under the IRDA Act, 1999.",
        "While RBI and SEBI are headquartered in Mumbai, IRDAI is headquartered in Hyderabad."
      ],
